{"_id":"68dcfa68166b018f83df7b50","roadmapSlug":"css","nodeId":"lo6OuD5hsZ7_r01jp-u0U","description":"# Color\n\nColor in CSS is used to specify the foreground color of text and other elements. It can be defined using various methods, including named colors (like \"red\" or \"blue\"), hexadecimal values (like \"#FF0000\"), RGB values (like \"rgb(255, 0, 0)\"), RGBA values (which include an alpha channel for transparency), HSL values (hue, saturation, lightness), and HSLA values (which include an alpha channel for HSL).","resources":[{"type":"article","title":"Text color","url":"https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/CSS/color","_id":"6a67293033d15c83102144a2"},{"type":"article","title":"CSS Font Color ΓÇô How to Style Text in HTML","url":"https://www.freecodecamp.org/news/css-font-color-how-to-style-text-in-html/","_id":"6a67293033d15c83102144a3"}],"createdAt":"2025-10-01T09:54:48.588Z","updatedAt":"2026-07-27T09:47:28.129Z","lessonPacks":[{"_id":"6a22adddac1c5fa9928ab3ab","title":"CSS Fundamentals","slug":"css","description":"Style, lay out, and debug real pages without fighting the cascade.","lessonIds":["6a15d62fac1c5fa9928a3fb6","6a15e1b0ac1c5fa9928a403f","6a16f11aac1c5fa9928a7c14","6a19dcdfac1c5fa9928a84a5","6a19e79cac1c5fa9928a8571","6a19f85cac1c5fa9928a8654","6a1d7a23ac1c5fa9928a8b4e","6a1dd2daac1c5fa9928a9884","6a1ecf18ac1c5fa9928a9a81","6a1f3245ac1c5fa9928a9cdd","6a20aa64ac1c5fa9928aa44a","6a20ba69ac1c5fa9928aa755","6a20c105ac1c5fa9928aa818","6a20c2e5ac1c5fa9928aa847","6a20c490ac1c5fa9928aa871","6a20c5adac1c5fa9928aa884","6a20c6a5ac1c5fa9928aa897","6a20c7c5ac1c5fa9928aa8aa","6a20ca2fac1c5fa9928aa8d0","6a20cb82ac1c5fa9928aa8e3"],"projectIds":["68b7185fffbff9183d772aed","68b7185fffbff9183d772aee","68b7185fffbff9183d772af0","68b7185fffbff9183d772af6","6a26960eac1c5fa9928acb63","6a26b431ac1c5fa9928acefa"],"featuredImage":"","readingTime":174,"lessonCount":20,"quizCount":0,"projectCount":6}],"paidResources":[],"contribution":"https://github.com/kamranahmed